From: NNdroid <99177648+NNdroid@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: amlogic: retain Ophub HK1 Box MMC numbering

The mainline G12 include numbers SD, eMMC and SDIO as mmc0, mmc1 and mmc2.
Existing Ophub installations use SDIO, SD and eMMC in that order. Preserve
the board's numbering so device-path root arguments and existing storage
scripts do not silently select another controller after a kernel update.
Override aliases on HK1 Box only; keep the shared Meson include unchanged.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-hk1box-vontar-x3.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-hk1box-vontar-x3.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-hk1box-vontar-x3.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-hk1box-vontar-x3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-sm1-hk1box-vontar-x3.dts
@@ -15,6 +15,12 @@
 	compatible = "amlogic,sm1";
 	model = "HK1 Box/Vontar X3";
 
+	aliases {
+		mmc0 = &sd_emmc_a; /* SDIO */
+		mmc1 = &sd_emmc_b; /* SD card */
+		mmc2 = &sd_emmc_c; /* eMMC */
+	};
+
 	memory@0 {
 		device_type = "memory";
 		reg = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0xFFFFFFFF>;
